# Platform Designer generated output. Each example's build.sh regenerates it
# from qsys/build_system.tcl and the .qsys file, both of which ARE tracked.
#
# For the SDRAM example this is more than tidiness: the generated tree contains
# Intel's controller RTL, which is not under this repository's MIT licence.
# Keeping it out of the repository is what makes example/ genuinely original
# work, as LICENSE and altera_avalon_new_sdram_controller/NOTICE both state.
**/qsys/*_sys/
*.sopcinfo

# The generated SDRAM memory model, produced by
# example/de10_lite_rtl/simulation/gen_mem_model.sh from your own Quartus
# installation. Intel's output, so it is not redistributed here either.
**/simulation/.gen/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# --- Local tooling config (Cowork / Claude Code) ---
.claude/
